00:07:40.082 --> 00:08:00.997
And I have a quote for that: If the unconscious attitude is too infantile, too immature, an old woman appears as a compensation figure, and the wise old man always appears when one is too foolish. Then the moment one becomes mature and reasonable in one's attitude, infantile figures turn up in dreams. The puer aeternus motive, for instance.

00:08:01.558 --> 00:08:24.542
You see, when one is old in one's consciousness, perhaps too reasonable, too adapted, too considerate, then one's soul is young. It is a child even, because one needs childlikeness in order not to dry up and suffocate in one's own wonderful adaption. So this is something to look out for. In Dreams, what are the kind of figures that gets encountered?

00:08:24.815 --> 00:08:46.007
Because the interesting thing is when you have figures in the unconscious, it is never something separated from oneself. It's one's own psyche. It's one's own unconscious. It is a representation of a part of oneself and very likely a part that is separated. It's so separated that it's being experienced as a separate entity.

00:08:46.926 --> 00:09:03.684
