00:09:29.642 --> 00:09:51.901
So you have the compensating figure and your consciousness is too adapted. So this means the puer aeternus archetype gets activated to bring the person back into balance. What can happen if the relationship is not built up in a sensible way? Compensation really tries to bring the person back in the middle.

00:09:52.014 --> 00:10:16.689
That means if the person stays in this adapted state, in this one-sided state, the other side will get stronger and stronger and stronger and push. And if it gets ignored completely, this can result in a possession, which which means the archetype basically takes over the body and the being of the person, also in waking life. This can happen voluntarily and involuntarily.

00:10:17.758 --> 00:10:37.967
Voluntarily would be then a kind of identification to say like, oh yeah, I'm now really this free-floating spirit that came up from my unconscious. So the awareness would be missing that there's actually something that is separated, something impersonal. That needs to be integrated, but then rather it's left out completely.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:11:00.212
So we have it then in the unconscious, and of course, what can also happen is when a person is just too infantile in general. This means, of course, everybody's growing up as first a child and has the psychology of a child.

00:11:00.592 --> 00:11:21.160
But this, of course, needs to change, and this needs to adapt to the circumstances to become collective, in a sense, to be adapted to the outside world. But of course, someone cannot stay there. And this is what Freud dealt with, to bring people out of their family psychology.

